# plakat house recipe — `--medium pen-ink`: the medium's accepted plan (the review cycles' verification set), read by
# `paint plan --director` / `paint from --make-plan` as the base the picture's facts adjust. Tune here, not in the source.
# plakat paint plan — pen and ink (7.12.0). Set 1: the pencil's drawing machinery (the light is the paper, the line
# traced along the picture's edges, the hatch straight along the form and at the hand's diagonal where there is no
# direction, the marks stopped at the contours, the tone in layers) borrowed through the plan for a steel nib and
# black ink: no grain (the ink fills the paper), no stump and no eraser (ink does not rub or lift), every line full
# black (nib), the tone by the number of lines. Set 2: pens of three sizes in layers, broad to fine (nibs).
# Set 3: the pens routed by the tone and the plane (nib_tone), the paper kept in the shadows (nib_white), the bone
# line in full black at a flat nib's hard edge. Set 4: the pen's accents after the bone — cast-shadow anchors
# (nib_anchor) and the shorthand dashes in the lights (nib_hint). Set 5: the face kept light (nib_face), the forms
# parted by paper (nib_gap), the folds modelled (nib_relief), the far ground fine (nib_far), the broad nib under the
# figure only (nib_occlude). Set 7: no gap and no relief on the fur. Set 8: the eyes kept and drawn (nib_eyes), the
# fur thinned (nib_fur), the figure's half-tones lifted (nib_lift), the contact shadow under it (nib_contact).
# Set 9: the figure in parallel hatching with its features and bold contours (nib_figure). Set 10: the hatching
# along the form in cells, the darks solid with the folds white, the face read against its own range.
# Set 11: the held umbrella outlined with the figure (nib_object), the near grass in tufts (nib_tuft), the figure's
# outline closed over its gaps (nib_close).
# Set 12: the dark grass merged into one mass (nib_mass), the figure's outline in a line of changing weight (nib_rim),
# the contact shadows solid black under it (nib_pool), the far planes kept to a few fine lines (nib_air).
# Set 13: every person found drawn as the figure, with or without a face (nib_people); the figure's tone
# read against the whole picture, so clothing light in its scene stays light (nib_value).
# Set 14: small faces with the finest pen (nib_fine_face), the grass found by CLIP and its tufts scattered in clumps
# (nib_scatter), the contact shadow solid only at the contact (nib_falloff), the far planes by depth (nib_depth).
# Set 15: the found grass grown thick by its darkness (nib_lush), the specular highlights kept white (nib_glint),
# the hand's waver doubled so a long line breathes.
medium: pen-ink
palette: sumi
style: legible
new: true
armature: 384
armature_face: 768
armature_body: 384
semantic: true
sam: true
families: true
commit_shadows: 0.0
shadow_floor: 0.16
detail_len: 0.5
# infill: where the picture has no direction the mark at the hand's diagonal
infill: 45
min_brush: 1.5
dry: 1.0
pickup: 0.0
bleed: 0.0
wash_in: 0.0
wet_cap: 0.2
scumble: 0.0
deplete: 0.0
granulate: 0.0
contour: 0.0
small: 400
small_min: 100
anchor: 0.15
trim: 0.5
hatch: 1.0
cross: 45
span: 0.6
edge: 0.6
umbra: 1.0
solid: 1.0
loose: 0.1
lost: 0.0
paper: 1.0
erase: 0.0
touch: 0.0
velvet: 0.08
velvet_dark: 0.25
paper_top: 1.0
paper_knee: 0.5
bone: 1.0
bone_coherence: 0.5
bone_ryaku: 0.3
bone_fade: 0.0
bone_wind: 0.5
weight: 1.0
slant: 1.0
clip: 0.6
tiers: 0.8
waver: 0.6
ma: 0.3
ma_focus: 0.4
ma_flow: 0.6
nib: 1.0          # a steel nib: every line full black, the tone by how many lines a cell takes, the width under the pass's nib
grade: 0.8        # the pen's lighter key: a dark orange fur drawn in lines over the paper, not a black mass
nibs: 3           # three pens in layers: a broad nib for the masses first, a middle one, a fine one for the detail last
nib_tone: 1.0     # each pen only where the tone is dark enough for its width, read against the eye's attention: the broad nib in the near deep shadows, the fine one on the far ground, the lights blank
nib_white: 0.2    # the deepest shadow keeps a fifth of the paper between its lines, not a flat black
nib_anchor: 1.0   # the cast-shadow touches under the figure, the stones and the tufts: crossed black clusters at the middle pen
nib_hint: 1.0     # the fine pen's rare short dashes in a sunlit passage with a sharp contrast of its own
nib_face: 1.0     # the face with the finest pen alone, its cheek and nose left to the paper
nib_gap: 0.4      # a sliver of paper along the long contours: the umbrella, the sleeve and the body parted
nib_relief: 0.6   # the hatching thinned on the form's highlights: the coat's folds modelled
nib_far: 0.5      # the sky and the far ground in the finest pen only, the far slope in light lines
nib_occlude: 1.0  # the broad nib only in the cast shadows under the figure
nib_eyes: 1.0     # an animal's eyes found by their catchlights, kept from the coat's hatching and drawn in pure black, the catchlight left white
nib_fur: 0.6      # the coat's half-tones and lit bulges lifted: the fur thins on the body, the dark markings kept
nib_lift: 1.0     # the figure's half-tones lifted: the coat and the face to their contours, the hatching in the deep folds
nib_contact: 1.0  # the cast shadow under the seated figure deepened to a contact patch, so it rests on the ground
nib_figure: 1.0   # the figure drawn as a pen draws it: hatching along the form, the darks closed to black with the folds white, the face left to the paper and its features drawn, bold contours
nib_object: 1.0   # the umbrella and the stick the figure holds: off the landscape's marks, hatched with the figure, their contours firm black
nib_tuft: 1.0   # the near grass as fans of blades from one root, doubled under the figure; the old marks there mostly dropped
nib_close: 1.0   # the figure's outline: a gap under a 40th of the sheet between two drawn stretches closed with a thin line
nib_mass: 1.0   # the dark grass: more tufts rooted anywhere in the cell, crossing into one dark mass
nib_rim: 1.0   # the figure's silhouette outlined in one line, swelling on the shadow side, parting it from the ground
nib_pool: 1.0   # the contact shadows under the figure and the umbrella closed to solid black with the broadest pen
nib_air: 1.0   # off the eye's attention the passes' marks thinned, the far hills a few fine lines
nib_people: 1.0   # every person the detector finds is the figure, a group whole, a back turned too
nib_value: 1.0   # the figure's tone read against the whole picture: clothes light in their scene stay light
nib_fine_face: 1.0   # a group's small faces with the finest pen, their eyes and noses traced
nib_scatter: 0.5   # the tufts in clumps and clearings, not on a grid
nib_falloff: 1.0   # the contact shadow black only where the figure meets the ground, then broken dashes fading out
nib_depth: 0.6   # the far hills and the horizon by the picture's depth: the finest pen, a few lines
nib_lush: 1.0   # the grass grown thick where it is dark, its clumps crossing into one deep mass
nib_glint: 1.0   # the specular highlights on metal, glass and glaze kept to the paper
micro: 0.5          # v5: the fine brushes come back where half the local contrast within their reach is lost
adapt: 0.5          # v5: the seed on the cell's strongest feature, the mark its extent, the flat cells withheld
point_field: 0.5    # v5: the ring round a point of light may hold 16% of bright pixels (needs `point` to act)
